/* THE PRACTICE :: FRONTIER AI
   Three immersive simulation modules set inside frontier AI laboratories.
   A — insider risk and model-weight custody under a RAND-style security level program.
   B — an agentic product that hit the lethal trifecta and moved real customer data.
   C — the CISO chair: dangerous-capability evals, thresholds, regulators, and publication.

   Grounding: RAND RR-A2849-1 Securing AI Model Weights (five security levels, 38 attack
   vectors); Anthropic Responsible Scaling Policy (ASL-3 activation, May 2025); Google
   DeepMind Frontier Safety Framework v3 (critical capability levels); OWASP Top 10 for LLM
   Applications 2025; Simon Willison, The Lethal Trifecta (16 June 2025); EchoLeak
   CVE-2025-32711 (Aim Security, June 2025; arXiv 2509.10540); Beurer-Kellner et al., Design
   Patterns for Securing LLM Agents against Prompt Injections (arXiv 2506.08837);
   Debenedetti et al., CaMeL (arXiv 2503.18813); Mandiant M-Trends 2025; Verizon DBIR 2026;
   United States v. Linwei Ding (N.D. Cal., conviction January 2026). */

